        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing patterns in this codebase:\n\n- `DuplicateEmailException` mirrors the sibling `DuplicateTelephoneException`/`CityOwnerLimitException` exceptions exactly (RuntimeException carrying the offending value in a `transient` field with a getter).\n- The new `@ExceptionHandler` in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` is a faithful copy of the adjacent handlers, using the same `detailBuild(...)`, 409 status, and `errors` property convention.\n- `requireUniqueEmail(...)` is structurally a twin of the pre-existing `requireUniqueTelephone(...)` (stream over `findAllOwners()`, null-filter, compare normalized form, throw), and its placement in `addOwner` \u2014 normalize, `requireUnique...`, then set \u2014 matches how telephone is handled two lines above. The `null`-email early return is consistent with `normalizeEmail`'s documented \"absent email is allowed\" contract.\n\nLogic is in the right unit (a private guard method alongside the other create-time uniqueness rules), nothing is duplicated beyond the deliberately repeated per-rule idiom already established here, and no class is being turned into a catch-all. A maintainer of this file would find it entirely natural."
